                                "sense_id": "728a7cd0-c1cc-3e06-9450-14a8c1765a8e",
                                "text": "The 81-year-old Saul Bellow’s slim novella “The Actual,”published^([sic]) three years before the heftier “Ravelstein,” distills his abiding attraction to “first-class noticers” into a Chicago romance with fairy-tale elements, in which a lifelong noticer is sought out and rewarded for his gift."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a9f1c999-17a0-48a8-a48d-7d21f51784f7",
                                "sense_id": "728a7cd0-c1cc-3e06-9450-14a8c1765a8e",
                                "text": "“He’s a great noticer of things, a great listener. His dialogue still sounds like real speech.”"
                            }
                        ]
